  "contentHtml": "\n                                    \n\n                                                                            <p><img src=\"https://health.economictimes.indiatimes.com/Themes/Release/theme4/images/icons/et-default-user.svg\" alt=\"Shimona Kanwar\">\n                                            \n                                        </p>\n                                                                        \n                                                                                    <ul>\n                                                                                                    <li>\n                                                                                                                                                                            <a>Shimona Kanwar</a>\n                                                            \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        \n                                                                                                            </li>\n                                                                                                                                                    <li><a href=\"/agency/87654367/TNN\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">TNN</a></li>\n                                                                                            </ul>\n                                                                                <ul>\n                                                                                            <li>Published On Aug 25, 2026 at 12:05 PM IST</li>\n                                                                                                                                </ul>\n                                    \n                                                                            \n                                                                        \n                                \n                                \n\n                    <!-- Display video article in news article for the custom next story -->\n                    \n                    <!-- Modifying the body placing embeds,promoslots,related etc.-->\n                                        <figure><img src=\"/images/default.jpg\" alt=\"\"></figure><p>Chandigarh: The Advanced Eye Centre at <a href=\"/tag/pgi\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">PGI</a> has reached a global benchmark in saving children’s sight, establishing itself as the world’s leading hub for specialised paediatric glaucoma care.According to documented medical literature, PGI has now officially overtaken the world-renowned Samuel and Ethel Balkan International <a href=\"/tag/pediatric+glaucoma\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Pediatric Glaucoma</a> Center at the <a href=\"/tag/bascom+palmer+eye+institute\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Bascom Palmer Eye Institute</a> in <a href=\"/tag/miami\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Miami</a>, previously recognised as the world’s only standalone paediatric glaucoma centre, to handle the largest volume of young patients.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>“While the Miami centre treats an average of 4,133 children annually, including 339 new patients, PGI managed 7,269 children in total and registered 602 new referrals during 2025-26, surpassing the Miami institute’s numbers,” Dr Sushmita Kaushik, professor and in-charge of glaucoma services at PGI, said.</p>\n                            <p>Advt\n                            </p>\n\n                              \n                                                         \n                        <p>This unprecedented patient volume was highlighted through a national study spearheaded by Dr Kaushik in her capacity as founder secretary of the <a href=\"/tag/indian+pediatric+glaucoma+society\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Indian Pediatric Glaucoma Society</a>. Tracking childhood glaucoma across 13 major medical centres in India, the study revealed that PGI treated the highest number of newly diagnosed cases in the country. Together with the <a href=\"/tag/lv+prasad+eye+institute\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">LV Prasad Eye Institute</a>, the two institutions accounted for more than half of all newly diagnosed children nationwide.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>What began in 2012 as a once-a-week clinic started by Dr Kaushik has, over the past 14 years, evolved into a major lifeline for families battling this rare, complex and potentially blinding eye disease.</p><p>“PGI’s exceptional clinical workload, pioneering research and contribution to global glaucoma care demonstrate how specialised expertise can transform outcomes for children with a potentially blinding disease. This is a matter of immense pride for PGI and, above all, represents a significant contribution towards preventing avoidable <a href=\"/tag/childhood+blindness\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">childhood blindness</a>,” said Prof Vivek Lal, director, PGI.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>PGI’s eye centre has also gained international recognition for performing the country’s first goniotomy, a delicate sight-saving surgery for infants, developing an affordable glaucoma drainage device for severe cases, pioneering advanced non-invasive laser imaging for early diagnosis, and leading groundbreaking genetic studies on infant eye health.                    </p><!-- Category Most Read Placement -->\n                                                                    \n                                                                \n                                <ul>\n                                                                            <!-- <li>By <span>Shimona Kanwar</span>,</li> -->\n                                    \n\n                                                                            <li>By\n                                                                                            <a>Shimona Kanwar</a>\n\n                                                                                                                                                                                        , \n                                                                                    </li>\n                                                                        <li><a href=\"/agency/87654367/TNN\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">TNN</a></li>\n                                </ul>\n                                <ul>\n                                    <!-- <li> Updated On Aug 25, 2026 at 12:05 PM IST</li> -->\n                                    <li>Published On Aug 25, 2026 at 12:05 PM IST</li>\n                                    <!-- <li class=\"desktop-view\">2 min read</li> -->\n                                </ul>\n                            \n                                        \n\n                    \n\n                    <!-- Comment Section -->\n                                            \n                                        <!-- Comment Section -->\n\n                    \n                      \n    \n            <p>\n                </p><h2>Join the community of 2M+ industry professionals. </h2>   \n                <h3>Subscribe to Newsletter to get latest insights &amp; analysis in your inbox.</h3>\n            <p></p>\n\n            <!-- <figure class=\"top-newsletter-subs__icon-nl\" role=\"presentation\" aria-label=\"Newsletter icon\">\n                <img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://st.etb2bimg.com/Themes/Release/theme4/images/icons/icon-newsletter.svg\" alt=\"Newsletter icon\" width=\"55\" height=\"55\">\n            </figure> -->\n        \n            \n            